 ## Background
-Voxel trilinear interpolation is a fundamental technique in volume rendering and computer graphics for sampling dense 3D grids [S5, unofficial]. The SIMD optimization leverages CPU vector instructions (like AVX) to accelerate the interpolation process, which is a bottleneck in real-time applications. The method is widely used in tools like `torchmcubes` for marching cubes on GPU [S2, unofficial], and in parallel volume renderers [S3, unofficial].
